==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/r̥eitn/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|eitn|lang=is}}
*: Homophones: {{l|is|Hreinn}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|hreinn}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*hrainiz}}.

====Adjective====
{{is-adj|hreinni|hreinastur}}

# [[clean]]
# [[pure]]
# {{lb|is|slang}} [[virgin]]
#: ''[[vera|Ertu]] [[ennþá]] '''hreinn'''?''
#:: [[be|Are]] [[you]] [[still]] a '''virgin'''? (referring to a man)
#: ''[[vera|Ertu]] [[ennþá]] '''hrein'''?''
#:: [[be|Are]] [[you]] [[still]] a '''virgin'''? (referring to a woman)

=====Inflection=====
{{is-decl-adj-3|hr|ei|n}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{sense|clean}} {{l|is|óhreinn}}, {{l|is|skítugur}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|hreinleiki}}
* {{l|is|hreinn sveinn}}
* {{l|is|hrein mey}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|hreinn}}.

====Noun====
{{is-noun|m|hreins|hreinar}}

# (male) [[reindeer]]

=====Declension=====
{{is-decl-noun-m-s1|hr|ei|n|n|i=i}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|is|hreindýr}}

