==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|non}} {{m|gem-pro|*hrinda-}}, akin to German {{m|de|Renn||reindeer}} and Old English {{m|ang|hran||reindeer}}, most likely from {{etyl|ine-pro|non}} {{m|ine-pro|*ḱer-}}.

===Noun===
{{non-noun|m|hreins|hreinar}}

# [[reindeer]]

====Declension====
{{non-decl-m-a|hrein|hrein|ns=hreinn}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|non|hreindýri}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|non|hreindýri}}
* {{l|non|hreinbjálbi}}
* {{l|non|hreinstaka}}

====Descendants====
{{top2}}
* Danish: {{l|da|ren}}
* Faroese: {{l|fo|rein-}} ({{l|fo|reindýr}}, {{l|fo|reindjór}})
* Icelandic: {{l|is|hreinn}}
{{mid2}}

* Norwegian (Nynorsk): {{l|nn|rein}}
* Norwegian (Bokmål): {{l|nb|rein}}
* Swedish: {{l|sv|ren}}
